      <h3>Our Commitment</h3>
      <p>
        Katryan Property Services Ltd handles client money in full compliance with the Client Money Protection (CMP)
        regulations. We are members of the <strong>UK ALA Client Money Protection Scheme</strong>, which protects client
        money held by us in the course of our estate agency and lettings management activities.
      </p>

      <div class="well">
        <h4>UK ALA Client Money Protection Scheme</h4>
        <p>
          Our membership of the UK ALA Client Money Protection Scheme means that client money held by us — including
          rent, deposits and other funds — is protected in the event of misappropriation. You can verify our membership
          and obtain a copy of our current certificate on request or by contacting the scheme directly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3>What Is Client Money?</h3>
      <p>
        Client money is any money that we hold on behalf of our clients in the course of our estate agency or property
        management activities. This includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Rent collected on behalf of landlords</li>
        <li>Security deposits held prior to registration with a government-approved tenancy deposit scheme</li>
        <li>Holding deposits</li>
        <li>Maintenance and repair funds held on behalf of landlords</li>
        <li>Sale proceeds and purchase deposits held during conveyancing</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How We Protect Client Money</h3>
      <p>We protect client money through the following measures:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>All client money is held in a dedicated client account, separate from our own business funds</li>
        <li>Client accounts are held with a UK-regulated bank or building society</li>
        <li>We maintain detailed records of all client money received, held and paid</li>
        <li>Regular reconciliation of client accounts is carried out</li>
        <li>Client money is not used for any purpose other than that for which it was received</li>
        <li>Where required by law, security deposits are transferred to a government-approved tenancy deposit
          protection scheme within the statutory time limit</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Tenancy Deposit Protection</h3>
      <p>
        In accordance with the Housing Act 2004 (as amended), all security deposits taken for Assured Shorthold
        Tenancies must be protected in a government-authorised tenancy deposit protection scheme within 30 days of
        receipt. We register deposits with an approved scheme and provide tenants with the required Prescribed
        Information within the same 30-day period.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work with the following government-approved schemes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tenancy Deposit Scheme (TDS)</li>
        <li>Deposit Protection Service (DPS)</li>
        <li>mydeposits</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Complaints About Client Money</h3>
      <p>
        If you have a concern about the handling of client money, please contact us in the first instance. We operate
        a formal complaints procedure and will acknowledge your complaint within three working days and provide a full
        written response within 15 working days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you remain dissatisfied, you may escalate your complaint to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The Property Ombudsman (TPO)</strong> — our independent redress scheme</li>
        <li><strong>UK ALA</strong> — our Client Money Protection scheme provider, in the event of a claim relating to
          misappropriation of client money</li>
      </ul>

